explanation:
This complete React/JSX example exposes whether a panel is open:
```react
function App() {
  const [open, setOpen] = React.useState(false);
  return <nav>
    <button aria-expanded={open} aria-controls="help-panel"
      onClick={() => setOpen(value => !value)}>
      Help
    </button>
    {open && <ul id="help-panel">
      <li><button>Read instructions</button></li>
    </ul>}
  </nav>;
}
```
At first, Help is collapsed and no list appears. Activating it shows the list and changes aria-expanded to true. aria-controls names the id of the controlled element. This exposes information; the attributes do not implement opening by themselves.

Replace the first App with this complete version:
```react
function App() {
  const [open, setOpen] = React.useState(false);
  const trigger = React.useRef(null);
